div></div>","info":{"doc":"The coefficient bound and the denominator `Grind.CommRing.Expr.majQ_k` of `e`, where the variables\nof `invs` denote the inverses of their numerals.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprMajQ","kind":"def","line":171,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprMajQ","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L171-L192"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.invLookup\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">invLookup</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">invs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> (<a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Var\">Var</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Var\">Var</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`Grind.CommRing.InvVars.lookup_k`: the search stops at the first larger variable.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.invLookup","kind":"def","line":165,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.invLookup","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L165-L169"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.kronLinExponent?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">kronLinExponent?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">l </span><span class=\"fn\">r</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.RingExpr\">RingExpr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">maxBits</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The exponent `K` of the linear Kronecker certificate (`Grind.CommRing.Expr.eq_of_kronLin`) for\n`l` and `r`, if they are linear and the values at the point stay below `maxBits` bits.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.kronLinExponent?","kind":"def","line":155,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.kronLinExponent?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L155-L163"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprLinCode\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">exprLinCode</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.RingExpr\">RingExpr</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"An upper bound on the codes of the values of `e` and its subterms at the point of the linear\ncertificates, where the variable `x` has code `x + 1` (`Grind.CommRing.Expr.toLin`). For a linear\n`e`, this is one more than its largest variable, but powers count, as in `exprMaxCode`: the kernel\nevaluates `x ^ k` in `(x ^ k) ^ 0`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprLinCode","kind":"def","line":141,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprLinCode","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L141-L153"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.kronExponent?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">kronExponent?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">norm </span><span class=\"fn\">maxCode </span><span class=\"fn\">maxBits</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The exponent `K` of a Kronecker certificate whose coefficients are bounded by `norm` and whose\nmonomials have codes at most `maxCode`, if the values at the point stay below `maxBits` bits: they\nhave about `K * maxCode` bits.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.kronExponent?","kind":"def","line":131,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.kronExponent?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L131-L139"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprMaxCode\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">exprMaxCode</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.RingExpr\">RingExpr</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"An upper bound on the packed codes of the monomials of the polynomials of `e` and its subterms.\nThe base of `a ^ 0` counts too, since the kernel evaluates it at the point.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprMaxCode","kind":"def","line":119,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprMaxCode","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L119-L129"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyMaxCode\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">polyMaxCode</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The largest packed code of the monomials of `p`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyMaxCode","kind":"def","line":114,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyMaxCode","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L114-L117"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.monCode\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">monCode</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Mon\">Mon</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The packed code of `m` in base `B` (`Grind.CommRing.Mon.code_k`).","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.monCode","kind":"def","line":109,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.monCode","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L109-L112"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyNorm1\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">polyNorm1</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The sum of the absolute values of the coefficients of `p` (`Grind.CommRing.Poly.norm1_k`).","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyNorm1","kind":"def","line":104,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyNorm1","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L104-L107"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyMaxDeg\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">polyMaxDeg</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The maximum degree of the monomials of `p` (`Grind.CommRing.Poly.maxDeg_k`).","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyMaxDeg","kind":"def","line":99,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.polyMaxDeg","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L99-L102"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprMajorant\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">exprMajorant</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.RingExpr\">RingExpr</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The coefficient bound `Grind.CommRing.Expr.majorant_k` of `e`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprMajorant","kind":"def","line":89,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprMajorant","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L89-L97"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprExpandsSum\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">exprExpandsSum</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.RingExpr\">RingExpr</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`true` if normalizing `e` multiplies out a sum: a product or power with a sum of nonconstant\nterms. Otherwise normalizing `e` only merges terms, and is cheaper than a Kronecker certificate.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprExpandsSum","kind":"def","line":76,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprExpandsSum","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.lean#L76-L87"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Arith/Kronecker.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.Arith.exprDegS\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">exprDegS</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">B</span> : <